<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Board details SAfrica's 96/97 maize stock position.</title>
<headline>Board details SAfrica's 96/97 maize stock position.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African Maize Board on Wednesday detailed the country's stock position for the 1996/1997 season following the final official crop, as follows:</p>
<p>(figures in thousands of tonnes)</p>
<p>						  White    Yellow    Total</p>
<p>    Stock carried over from 1995/6    294	301	 595</p>
<p>Plus -</p>
<p>    Total 1996/97 crop		    5,571    4,177     9,928</p>
<p>Less -</p>
<p>    Retentions				711	833	 1,544</p>
<p>Plus -</p>
<p>    Imports				   150	95	  245</p>
<p>    Total available in South Africa   5,484    3,740     9,224</p>
<p>Less -</p>
<p>    Domestic consumption		  3,500    2,600     6,100</p>
<p>    Export sales*			   1,400    1,294     2,694</p>
<p>    Total utilisation		     4,900    3,894     8,794</p>
<p>    Ending stocks			   584	-154	430</p>
<p>*It said export sales could be divided up as follows:</p>
<p>Sales by the Maize Board</p>
<p>    - Direct for export		   341	475	 816</p>
<p>    - To permit holders		   319	26	  345</p>
<p>    - Expected further sales	    164	53	  217</p>
<p>    - Exports by private trade	  576	740	 1,316</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
